1.text:
After 34.Kg5 Black mates at once.

The knight on e5 delivers the check

Nf3+

e5–f3 is a legal knight move and f3 is vacant after 31…Ne5+.  The check is on
g5

* g6 is occupied by …g6 and defended by …h7;
* f5 and h5 are covered by …g6;
* h4 and h6 are covered by Rh2;
* g4 is covered by the black bishop/rook complex;
* f4 is occupied by W Nf4;
* f6 is opened on the c3–d4–e5–f6 diagonal by the move …Nf3 and is covered
  once the knight leaves e5.

The checking knight on f3 cannot be captured or interposed and Kg5 has no
legal flight square.  The mate is therefore mate in one and is shorter than
any h6+ forcing continuation.

Nf3#

