1.text:
After 34.Kg5 Black is to move and the e5–f3 knight move is legal and is
check.

34... Nf3+

e5–f3 is a knight check on g5 and a knight check cannot be interposed.
The checking knight on f3 cannot be taken by Kg5, Qa5, Rd8 or Nf4 and
f3 is vacant after 31...Ne5+.

Kg5 has no flight:

* g6 is occupied/defended by …Pg6/h7;
* f5/h5 are covered by …Pg6;
* h4/h6 are covered by Rh2;
* g4 is covered by the black rook/bishop complex;
* f4 is occupied by Nf4;
* f6 is covered on the c3–d4–e5–f6 diagonal opened by …Nf3.

The king is therefore mated on the move and any h6+ forcing line is
≥2 plies, i.e. strictly longer than the immediate mate.

Shortest forced mate: Nf3#

